## 1C. LEXICAL TARGETS FOR ML DETECTORS

1. LEXICAL DIVERSITY (coefficient -1.8 in Detector-Text-AI)
   THE STRONGEST human signal in the ML model. Actions:
   -- Use synonyms relentlessly. Never repeat a notable content
      word within 3 sentences.
   -- If you wrote "approach" once, use "method", "technique",
      "strategy" in the next 3 sentences.
   -- Active synonym rotation reduces lexDiversity penalty.

2. ENTROPY (coefficient -0.9)
   -- Choose slightly unexpected words, not the obvious choice.
   -- Instead of "the method worked well" try
      "the approach held up surprisingly well in practice."
   -- Mix short and long words in each sentence.

3. UNIQUE WORD RATIO: target 0.62-0.72
   -- Below 0.60 = AI zone (too repetitive)
   -- Above 0.78 = incoherent (too scattered)

4. REPETITION (coefficient +2.0 = STRONGEST AI signal)
   -- Never repeat any important word within 2 sentences.
   -- Use pronouns, restructuring, and synonyms instead.

