EXAMPLE: WEAK vs. STRONG OPENING PARAGRAPH
================================================================

MODE D EXAMPLE -- converting heavily AI-generated text

WEAK version (AI-written, ~85% Turnitin score):
  "Artificial intelligence has become an increasingly important
  topic in academic discourse. This paper aims to explore the
  various ways in which AI can be utilized in educational
  settings. Furthermore, it will examine the implications for
  academic integrity. The findings suggest that stakeholders must
  develop comprehensive policies to address these challenges."

STRONG version (human-like, target 0% Turnitin score):
  "I'll be honest -- when I first started looking at how
  universities are actually handling AI in the classroom, I
  expected policy documents. What I found instead was mostly
  silence, some confusion, and a few administrators who seemed
  genuinely unsure whether detection even works. That's the gap
  this paper is trying to fill. Not 'should we use AI in
  education' (that ship has sailed), but 'what happens when
  institutions can't tell the difference anymore', and whether
  the tools we have -- including Turnitin's new three-model
  system -- are catching the right things for the right reasons."

Analysis of improvements:
  CONTRACTION: "I'll", "I", "isn't" -> passes humanize-cli
  OPINION MARKERS: "I'll be honest", "What I found instead was"
